mouse-aimbot third-party notices
==============================

This project stands on TargetFinder. Detection and the click-through overlay
approach are theirs; magnetic snap behavior is ours.

TargetFinder Toolkit
--------------------
Authors: Ahmed Ben Akouche, Géry Casiez, Mathieu Nancel, Julien Gori
License: MIT (Copyright (c) 2025 — see their LICENSE)
GitHub:  https://github.com/ahmedbenakouche/target_finder_toolkit
PyPI:    https://pypi.org/project/target-finder-toolkit/
Docs:    https://target-finder-toolkit.netlify.app/

Paper:
  Ahmed Ben Akouche, Géry Casiez, Mathieu Nancel, and Julien Gori. 2026.
  TargetFinder: Detecting Widgets from Pixels on Desktop Interfaces.
  arXiv:2607.19907. https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.19907

Dataset / models (from the paper release):
  https://osf.io/fr6y4/
  https://huggingface.co/ab-dev26/targetfinder

What we reuse
  - Runtime dependency on the published toolkit (widget YOLO models + detector API)
  - PyQt6 overlay pattern adapted from their demo
    (FramelessWindowHint, WindowStaysOnTopHint, WindowTransparentForInput,
    WA_TranslucentBackground)

What is original to mouse-aimbot
  - Magnetic / soft-aim cursor snap toward detected widgets
  - Force-quit hotkey, launch scripts, packaging

